              "question": "<p>Ethanol (the alcohol that is in wine and beer) is metabolised by zero order kinetics meaning that it is initially metabolised in a linear way, with about one standard drink metabolised per hour. But after it has been metabolised to the point that there is only about &lt; 1 standard drink, it is metabolised by first order kinetics.&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p>Given that, how long would it take a P plater to metabolise 3 standard drinks to the point that they have 0 blood alcohol?</p>\n"
            },
